        answer: 'This happens when you turn on hot water briefly, then turn it off, then on again quickly. The unit heats the water in the exchanger, but there\'s still cool water in the pipe between the heater and the tap. When you turn it back on, you briefly get leftover hot water, then cold water from the lines, then hot again as the unit fires up. It\'s a characteristic of how tankless units work rather than a malfunction.',
