    serviceDescription: 'Slab leak repair involves several steps. First, the leak is located using acoustic detection and thermal imaging to minimize the area that needs to be accessed. Then the contractor will present repair options: direct access (cutting through the slab above the leak), pipe rerouting (running a new pipe above the slab and through walls, bypassing the damaged section entirely), or in some cases epoxy pipe lining (coating the interior of the pipe to seal pinhole leaks). Each option has tradeoffs in cost, disruption, and longevity. Pipe rerouting is often preferred for older copper lines prone to future failures.',
