        question: 'What\'s the difference between slab repair and pipe rerouting?',
        answer: 'Slab repair (also called direct access repair) involves breaking through the concrete above the leak, repairing or replacing the damaged pipe section, and patching the concrete. It\'s less invasive but only addresses the specific failure point. Pipe rerouting abandons the slab-embedded pipe entirely and runs a new pipe through the walls and attic. It\'s more work upfront but eliminates the risk of future failures in that section of pipe.',
